---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: One package for Chrome, Edge and Firefox
    accDescr: The release builds one zip from extension/, with one manifest.json. Chrome 140 and newer, and Edge 140 and newer, run background.js as the service worker that background.service_worker names, and ignore the keys of Firefox. Firefox 140 and newer runs the same background.js from background.scripts, under the id of browser_specific_settings.gecko, and shows at the install that the add-on sends authentication data to Autodarts. scripts/check-manifest.mjs checks that both keys name background.js and that the data matches store/permissions.json, and addons-linter, the linter of addons.mozilla.org, finds no error in the package.

    checks["scripts/check-manifest.mjs and addons-linter<br>in scripts/check.sh"]
    zip["One zip from extension/<br>with one manifest.json"]
    chrome["Chrome 140 and newer<br>and Edge 140 and newer"]
    firefox["Firefox 140 and newer"]
    worker["background.js as the service worker,<br>from background.service_worker"]
    page["The same background.js as an event page,<br>from background.scripts"]
    gecko["The id of the add-on and the data that it sends,<br>from browser_specific_settings.gecko"]

    checks --> zip
    zip --> chrome --> worker
    zip --> firefox --> page
    firefox --> gecko

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class checks bot
    class worker,page done
